0.08249999999999999, 0.08249999999999999, 0.08249999999999999, 0.08249999999999999], "mean_per_gen": [0.03375, 0.0390625, 0.05375, 0.0596875, 0.0596875], "champion": {"genome": {"base": 3, "lsb": 1, "w": [0.5649816207436229, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}, "fitness": 0.08249999999999999}}}, "findings": {"radix": "<b>Write the least significant digit first.</b> It wins in every base: at 2<sup>15</sup> bits, base 4 LSB-first gets 87% of unseen sums and MSB-first 27%. Base 4 needs the fewest bits to reach 50% (about 16k), ahead of base 10 (19k). Binary, the Arecibo choice, is the worst positional system: written MSB-first it never reaches 50%. <b>The best numerals depend on the mind:</b> LSTMs given unary tally marks answer 83% of unseen sums after hearing just 41 examples, while every positional system leaves them at chance.", "content": "<b>Nothing teaches addition except sums.</b> Accuracy is predicted almost exactly by how many sums fit in the message. Counting, the traditional opener, gives no head start. Products, which look just like sums, cost a further 8\u201311 points. The other skills are learned on their own (89% of comparisons and 83% of products at 2<sup>16</sup> bits), but they do not transfer.", "channel": "<b>Framing is everything.</b> Given the same 2<sup>16</sup> bits as raw 5-bit codewords instead of symbols, no receiver learned to add (about 1% even on sums it heard, with no noise and no repetition), against 91% when symbol boundaries are given. With every condition at the floor, noise and repetition coding cannot be compared. A receiver that must first find the symbols needs far more than this budget.", "decipher": "<b>Five of twelve shuffled messages were read back completely</b>: base, digit values, digit order, +, \u00d7 and the comparison with its three outcomes. Both base-4 receivers are among them, and in each case the recovered + makes 100% of the decoded sums true. Digits and the separator were found exactly in every base up to 10. Receivers that understood poorly (base 3, MSB first: 27\u201330% of unseen sums) could not be read. Base 16 failed in the probe, not in the mind: its receivers score 81%, but only digits 0\u20137 ever lead a numeral and the role step missed the other nine."}}